---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
---

<Layout title="ISHARA">
<section>
<h1>OVERVIEW</h1>
<p>
  <strong>Key characteristics</strong><br>
  Touch-free: control slides from across the room.<br>
  Hardware-light: a standard webcam is all you need.<br>
  Deliberate by design: a lock mechanism and hold-to-trigger gestures prevent accidental commands.<br>
  Platform-agnostic output: sends standard keyboard commands, so it works with Google Slides and PowerPoint.<br>
</p>
</section>
<section>
<p>
  <strong>How it works</strong><br>
  Gesture Presenter is a compact Python application built on three well-proven libraries:
  <br>MediaPipe handles hand tracking and landmark detection.
  <br>OpenCV captures and displays the webcam feed.
  <br>PyAutoGUI sends the keystrokes that drive your slideshow.
</p>
<br>It uses OpenCV (cv2) to capture webcam video feeds, <br>MediaPipe (mediapipe) for 
    real-time hand tracking and landmark extraction, and <br>PyAutoGUI (pyautogui) to simulate keyboard shortcuts for slide navigation.
    It includes a security/safety locking mechanism ("armed" state via fist-holding) to prevent accidental gesture triggers.
</p>
</section>
</Layout>

<style>
  h1 {
    font-size: 34px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .subtitle {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .post-list {
    list-style: none;
  }

  .post-list li {
    padding: 24px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .post-list a {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .post-title {
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .post-title:hover {
    color: var(--link);
  }

  .post-date {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 13px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-left: 16px;
  }

  .post-excerpt {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 15px;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }

  .empty {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-top: 32px;
  }
</style>
